{"body":{"matters":"the balance between a part's self-keeping and its being directed","parts":[{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G2000012"},{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G200001A"},{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G200001R"},{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G2000020"}],"prose":"Everything in this space circles one balance: how much of itself a part may keep while something larger coordinates it. The answer is given as distribution of authority, yet a single highest holder keeps coming back, and the text itself shows the strain of holding so many pieces together.","title":"Keeping oneself while being held"},"id":"1M6YBY3G2000011","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000K"]}
