{"body":{"matters":"reliance on encoded knowledge","parts":[{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G10000CA"},{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G10003VP"},{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G10004EW"},{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G10004H6"},{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G10004PV"},{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G10004RR"},{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G10004V7"},{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G100050V"},{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G10008NE"},{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G10008WD"},{"$holds":true,"$ref":"1M6YBY3G1000BDC"}],"prose":"Ethics, understanding, bias and translation are each to be handled by writing down a structured vocabulary, which makes vocabulary-building the recurring unpaid cost.","title":"Ontology as the answer to everything"},"id":"1M6YBY3G200001E","instance":["1M6YBY3G000000K"]}
